IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `bnra-types`

-- Business Names Registration Act 2014, Part 2, ss 5 to 14: the requirement to
-- register, the application, the Registrar's decision, authorised representatives,
-- cancellation and expiry.  Source: source/BNRA2014.txt lines 380 to 789.
--
-- Where the Registrar "may", the rule answers whether the power is available on the
-- facts, never whether it will be exercised.  Regulations the Act relies on (the
-- prescribed particulars, fees, the prescribed late penalty) are inputs, not encoded.

§ `Part 2 -- Registration`

§§ `5. Requirement to register`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 5(1)"
GIVEN r IS A `Registration Requirement Facts`
      `the person is required to be registered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person and the business name were registered before the person carried on business` IF
        NOT `the person is required to be registered`
     OR NOT r's `the person carries on business in Singapore`
     OR (    r's `the person is registered`
         AND r's `the person's business name is registered`)

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 5(2)"
GIVEN r IS A `Registration Requirement Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `there is a separate registration for each business name` IF
    r's `the number of separate registrations` AT LEAST r's `the number of business names the person intends to carry on business under`

§§ `6. Manner and particulars of registration`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 6(1)(b)(iv), (vi)(A) and (vii)"
GIVEN p IS A `Personal Particulars`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the personal particulars are complete` IF
        p's `the full name is stated`
    AND p's `the identification is stated`
    AND p's `the nationality is stated`
    AND p's `the residential address is stated`
    AND p's `the contact address is stated`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 6(1)(b)(i) to (ix)"
GIVEN a IS AN `Application Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the application contains the particulars section 6(1)(b) requires` IF
        a's `the business name is stated`
    AND a's `the general nature of the business is stated`
    AND a's `the principal place of business is stated`
    AND a's `the date or proposed date of commencement of business is stated`
    AND a's `the other information that is prescribed is given`
    AND (CONSIDER a's `kind of registrant`
         WHEN `an individual proprietor` THEN `the personal particulars are complete` (a's `the particulars of the individual proprietor`)
         WHEN `a company that is a sole proprietor` THEN a's `the corporate name, registration number and registered office of the sole proprietor are stated`
         WHEN `a limited liability partnership that is a sole proprietor` THEN a's `the corporate name, registration number and registered office of the sole proprietor are stated`
         WHEN `a foreign company that is a sole proprietor` THEN a's `the corporate name, registration number and registered office of the sole proprietor are stated`
         WHEN `a firm` THEN
                 all `the personal particulars are complete` (a's `the particulars of every partner who is an individual`)
             AND a's `the corporate name, registration number and registered office of every partner that is a corporation are stated`)
    AND all `the personal particulars are complete` (a's `the particulars of every authorised representative, if any`)

-- 6(3): who is an "appropriate person" to lodge the application.

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 6(3)(a) to (f)"
GIVEN k IS A `Kind of Registrant`
      r IS A `Lodger Role`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is an appropriate person` IF
        r EQUALS `a registered corporate service provider authorised by and acting for the person`
     OR (CONSIDER k
         WHEN `an individual proprietor` THEN r EQUALS `the individual proprietor`
         WHEN `a company that is a sole proprietor` THEN r EQUALS `a director or a secretary of the company`
         WHEN `a limited liability partnership that is a sole proprietor` THEN r EQUALS `a manager of the limited liability partnership`
         WHEN `a foreign company that is a sole proprietor` THEN r EQUALS `an authorised representative of the foreign company, as section 366 of the Companies Act 1967 defines it`
         WHEN `a firm` THEN
                 r EQUALS `a partner of the firm who is an individual`
              OR r EQUALS `a director or a secretary of a company that is a partner of the firm`
              OR r EQUALS `a manager of a limited liability partnership that is a partner of the firm`
              OR r EQUALS `an authorised representative of a foreign company that is a partner of the firm`)

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 6(1)(a)"
GIVEN a IS AN `Application Facts`
      r IS A `Lodger Role`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the application is properly lodged` IF
        a's `the application is lodged with the Registrar`
    AND `the person is an appropriate person` (a's `kind of registrant`) r

-- 6(2): the Registrar may require verification of the application: a power with no
-- condition, inert.

§§ `7. Registration by nominee or trustee`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 7(1)"
GIVEN n IS A `Nominee Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the nominee or trustee has provided the particulars section 7(1) requires` IF
        NOT n's `the person carries on business wholly or mainly as nominee or trustee of or for another person`
     OR (    n's `the person has provided the particulars section 6 requires`
         AND n's `the person has provided the further particulars that are prescribed`)

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 7(2)"
GIVEN n IS A `Nominee Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person contravenes section 7(2)` IF
        n's `the person carries on business wholly or mainly as nominee or trustee of or for another person`
    AND n's `the other person is a foreign company`

§§ `8. Registration`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 8(1), (5) and s 9(a) to (c)"
GIVEN d IS A `Registration Decision Facts`
GIVETH A `Registration Outcome`
`the Registrar's duty on an application for registration` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT d's `an application for registration under section 6 has been received`
            THEN `there is no application to decide`
        IF     d's `the Registrar is satisfied that the business is likely to be used for an unlawful purpose or for purposes prejudicial to public peace, welfare or good order in Singapore`
            OR d's `the Registrar is satisfied that it would be contrary to the national security or interest for the person to be registered`
            OR (    d's `the person is a foreign company`
                AND NOT d's `the foreign company is registered under Division 2 of Part 11 of the Companies Act 1967`)
            OR (    d's `the business name is one the Registrar must refuse under section 17`
                AND NOT d's `the Minister has consented to registration under the business name`)
            THEN `the Registrar must refuse to register`
        IF NOT d's `the Registrar is satisfied with the particulars and other information provided`
            THEN `the Registrar is not required to register`
        OTHERWISE `the Registrar must register the applicant and the business name and issue a notice of registration`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 8(2)"
GIVEN c IS A `Certificate Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar may issue a certificate of confirmation of registration` IF
        c's `the person is registered under section 8(1)`
    AND c's `the person has lodged an application for a certificate of confirmation of registration`
    AND c's `the prescribed fee has been paid`

-- 8(3): every registration is valid for the period the Registrar specifies, and is
-- renewable for the period the Registrar approves.  The period is the Registrar's to
-- specify: inert.

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 8(3) and (4)"
GIVEN r IS A `Renewal Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar may refuse to renew because additional particulars were not provided` IF
        r's `the Registrar required additional particulars or information`
    AND NOT r's `the additional particulars or information were provided`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 8(5)"
GIVEN r IS A `Renewal Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar is not required to renew the registration` IF
    NOT r's `the Registrar is satisfied with the particulars and other information provided`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 8(3), (4) and (5)"
GIVEN r IS A `Renewal Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the registration is renewable` IF
        r's `the person has lodged an application for renewal`
    AND r's `the prescribed fee has been paid`
    AND NOT `the Registrar may refuse to renew because additional particulars were not provided` r
    AND NOT `the Registrar is not required to renew the registration` r

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 8(6)"
`registration or renewal implies that the person has complied with the law relating to the business` MEANS FALSE

-- 8(7), 12(4), 16(5), 17(9): appeal to the Minister, whose decision is final.

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 8(7), 16(5) and 17(9)"
GIVEN a IS AN `Appeal Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appeal is made within 30 days after notification` IF
    a's `the date of the appeal` AT MOST a's `the date the person was notified or informed of the decision` PLUS 30

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 8(7) and s 13(2)"
GIVEN a IS AN `Appeal Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person may appeal to the Minister within 30 days` IF
        a's `the person is aggrieved by the decision`
    AND `the appeal is made within 30 days after notification` a
    AND NOT a's `the decision is one to which the provision excludes an appeal because it rests on the Minister's certificate`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 12(4) and s 13(3)"
GIVEN a IS AN `Appeal Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person may appeal to the Minister within 30 days or a further period the Minister allows` IF
        a's `the person is aggrieved by the decision`
    AND (   `the appeal is made within 30 days after notification` a
         OR (CONSIDER a's `the date to which the Minister has allowed a further period, if any`
             WHEN JUST allowed THEN a's `the date of the appeal` AT MOST allowed
             WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE))
    AND NOT a's `the decision is one to which the provision excludes an appeal because it rests on the Minister's certificate`

§§ `9. When registration must be refused`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 9(a), (b), (c) and s 13(1)"
GIVEN p IS A `Public Interest Facts`
      `the person is a foreign company not registered under Division 2 of Part 11 of the Companies Act 1967` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar must refuse to register under section 9` IF
        p's `the Registrar is satisfied that the business is likely to be used, or is used or intended to be used, for an unlawful purpose or for purposes prejudicial to public peace, welfare or good order in Singapore`
     OR p's `the Registrar is satisfied that it would be contrary to the national security or interest`
     OR p's `the Minister for internal security has issued a certificate stating that he or she is satisfied of that`
     OR `the person is a foreign company not registered under Division 2 of Part 11 of the Companies Act 1967`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 13(1)"
GIVEN p IS A `Public Interest Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the certificate is conclusive evidence that it would be contrary to the national security or interest` IF
    p's `the Minister for internal security has issued a certificate stating that he or she is satisfied of that`

§§ `10. Registration does not confer ownership`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 10(1)"
`registration confers property in the registered business name or in a word in it` MEANS FALSE

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 10(2)"
`registration is evidence that the person owns property or a right or interest in property used for the business` MEANS FALSE

§§ `11. Authorised representative`

-- 11(14): whether a person resides outside Singapore.

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 11(14)(a) and (b)"
GIVEN r IS A `Residence Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person resides outside Singapore` IF
    IF r's `the person is a corporation`
    THEN r's `the corporation is incorporated or formed outside Singapore`
    ELSE r's `the individual's residential address is outside Singapore`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 11(1)"
GIVEN q IS A `Representative Requirement Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an authorised representative must be appointed` IF
        (CONSIDER q's `kind of registrant`
         WHEN `an individual proprietor` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `a firm` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `a foreign company that is a sole proprietor` THEN TRUE
         OTHERWISE FALSE)
    AND NOT null (q's `the individual proprietor, the partners of the firm or the officers of the foreign company, as the case may be`)
    AND all `the person resides outside Singapore` (q's `the individual proprietor, the partners of the firm or the officers of the foreign company, as the case may be`)

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 11(2) and (16)"
GIVEN q IS A `Representative Qualification Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person qualifies as an authorised representative` IF
        q's `the person is a natural person`
    AND q's `the person's age in years` AT LEAST 18
    AND q's `the person is otherwise of full legal capacity`
    AND q's `the person is ordinarily resident in Singapore`

-- 11(3), (4), (11): the last day for appointing.  At registration: at the time of
-- registration, or, if the business will be carried on from a later date, not later
-- than the date it commences.  After registration, and where the sole authorised
-- representative ceases: within 30 days after the event.

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 11(3), (4) and (11)"
GIVEN t IS AN `Appointment Trigger`
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for appointing an authorised representative` MEANS
    CONSIDER t
    WHEN `residing outside Singapore at the time of registration` registered commences THEN
        IF commences GREATER THAN registered THEN commences ELSE registered
    WHEN `ceasing to reside in Singapore after registration` ceased THEN ceased PLUS 30
    WHEN `the sole authorised representative ceasing` ceased THEN ceased PLUS 30

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 11(3), (4) and (11)"
GIVEN t IS AN `Appointment Trigger`
      `the date of appointment` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the authorised representative is appointed in time` IF
    `the date of appointment` AT MOST `the last day for appointing an authorised representative` t

-- 11(4) and (11) are duties with a 30-day deadline: regulative rules.

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 11(4)"
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party under the Act` `Act under the Act`
`the duty to appoint an authorised representative after ceasing to reside in Singapore` MEANS
    PARTY `The registrant`
    MUST `appoint an authorised representative`
    WITHIN 30
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `The registrant` BECAUSE "no authorised representative was appointed within 30 days after ceasing to reside in Singapore, as section 11(4) requires"

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 11(11)"
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party under the Act` `Act under the Act`
`the duty to appoint a new authorised representative` MEANS
    PARTY `The registrant`
    MUST `appoint a new authorised representative`
    WITHIN 30
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `The registrant` BECAUSE "no new authorised representative was appointed within 30 days after the sole authorised representative ceased, as section 11(11) requires"

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 11(7)"
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party under the Act` `Act under the Act`
`the duty to lodge notice of the appointment of an authorised representative` MEANS
    PARTY `The registrant`
    MUST `lodge a notice of the appointment of, and the consent of, the authorised representative`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `The registrant` BECAUSE "the notice of appointment and consent was not lodged within 14 days after the appointment, as section 11(7) requires"

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 11(9)"
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party under the Act` `Act under the Act`
`the duty to lodge notice that an authorised representative has ceased` MEANS
    PARTY `The registrant`
    MUST `lodge a notice that the authorised representative has ceased to be, or ceased to be qualified to be, the authorised representative`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `The registrant` BECAUSE "the notice that the authorised representative had ceased was not lodged within 14 days after that event, as section 11(9) requires"

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 11(8)"
GIVEN `the notice states the authorised representative's residential address` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the authorised representative's contact address` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the notice of appointment contains what section 11(8) requires` IF
        `the notice states the authorised representative's residential address`
    AND `the notice states the authorised representative's contact address`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 11(10)"
GIVEN `the registrant failed to lodge the notice under section 11(9)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the former authorised representative may lodge the notice` IF
    `the registrant failed to lodge the notice under section 11(9)`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 11(5)"
GIVEN l IS A `Representative Liability Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the authorised representative is personally responsible for the obligation` IF
    l's `the date the obligation attached to the registrant` AT LEAST l's `the date of the authorised representative's appointment`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 11(6)"
GIVEN l IS A `Representative Liability Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the authorised representative is subject to the same responsibilities, liabilities and penalties as the registrant` IF
        `the authorised representative is personally responsible for the obligation` l
    AND l's `the obligation has been defaulted on`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 11(12)"
GIVEN o IS A `Representative Offence Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the registrant is guilty of an offence under section 11(12)` IF
        o's `the registrant fails to comply with the requirement to appoint an authorised representative under section 11(1)`
     OR o's `the registrant fails to lodge the notice under section 11(7)`
     OR o's `the registrant fails to lodge the notice under section 11(9)`

-- 11(13) defines "officer" of a foreign company, 11(15) says a company or limited
-- liability partnership ceases to reside in Singapore when dissolved: both fix who is
-- listed in `Representative Requirement Facts` and when the date of ceasing falls, so
-- add no condition of their own: inert.

§§ `12. General power to cancel registration`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 12(1)(a)(i) and (ii), and s 13(1)"
GIVEN p IS A `Public Interest Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 12(1)(a) is satisfied` IF
        p's `the Registrar is satisfied that the business is likely to be used, or is used or intended to be used, for an unlawful purpose or for purposes prejudicial to public peace, welfare or good order in Singapore`
     OR p's `the Registrar is satisfied that it would be contrary to the national security or interest`
     OR p's `the Minister for internal security has issued a certificate stating that he or she is satisfied of that`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 12(1)(a), (b), (c) and (2)"
GIVEN g IS A `Cancellation Grounds Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `there is a ground for cancellation under section 12(1) or (2)` IF
        `section 12(1)(a) is satisfied` (g's `public interest facts`)
     OR g's `in connection with the person's business, the person carrying on the business, or another person appointed to manage it solely or substantially on that person's behalf, has been convicted of an offence under the Charities Act 1994`
     OR g's `the person required to appoint an authorised representative failed to appoint one within the period required under section 11(3) or (4)`
     OR g's `the person failed to appoint a new authorised representative within 30 days after the sole authorised representative ceased to be, or ceased to be qualified to be, the authorised representative`
     OR g's `the Central Provident Fund Board has notified the Registrar that the person is a member of the Central Provident Fund and has failed to comply with section 9A of the Central Provident Fund Act 1953`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 12(3)(a), (b) and (c)"
GIVEN p IS A `Cancellation Procedure Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the procedure of section 12(3) has been followed` IF
        p's `the Registrar gave the person notice in writing of the intention to cancel`
    AND p's `the number of days the notice specified for written representations` AT LEAST 30
    AND p's `the Registrar considered the written representations, if any, received within the time specified`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 12"
GIVEN g IS A `Cancellation Grounds Facts`
      p IS A `Cancellation Procedure Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar may cancel the registration under section 12` IF
        `there is a ground for cancellation under section 12(1) or (2)` g
    AND `the procedure of section 12(3) has been followed` p

§§ `13. Supplemental provision to sections 9 and 12`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 13(2) and (3)"
GIVEN `the decision rests on the certificate of the Minister for internal security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is a refusal under section 9(b) or a cancellation under section 12(1)(a)(ii)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appeal to the Minister is excluded` IF
        `the decision rests on the certificate of the Minister for internal security`
    AND `the decision is a refusal under section 9(b) or a cancellation under section 12(1)(a)(ii)`

§§ `14. Cancellation for failure to renew registration`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 14(1)"
GIVEN e IS AN `Expiry Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar is to give written notice that the registration may be cancelled unless renewed` IF
    e's `the registration has expired`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 14(2)"
GIVEN e IS AN `Expiry Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the period stated in the notice is long enough` IF
    e's `the last day of the period stated in the notice` AT LEAST e's `the date of the notice` PLUS 30

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 14(3)"
GIVEN e IS AN `Expiry Facts`
      `the date the Registrar proposes to cancel` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar may cancel for failure to renew` IF
        e's `the Registrar gave written notice that the registration may be cancelled unless renewed within the period stated`
    AND `the period stated in the notice is long enough` e
    AND NOT e's `the registration was renewed within the period stated`
    AND `the date the Registrar proposes to cancel` GREATER THAN e's `the last day of the period stated in the notice`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 14(4)"
GIVEN e IS AN `Expiry Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person and the business name continue to be registered after expiry` IF
        e's `the registration has expired`
    AND NOT e's `the registration has been cancelled`
